course: dictionary
lesson: 12427
title: Words about business and trust
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Dealings» is a plural noun. It means the business or contact that people or groups have with each other. «My dealings with the bank took all morning» means all the business I had with the bank that morning.
explain: The word can also tell you how someone behaves in business. «Honest dealings» means fair and truthful business. «Shady dealings» means business that may be dishonest or done in secret.
explain: Check the context clues. If the sentence says «secret» or «shady», the dealings are probably dishonest. To test your meaning, swap in «business» or «contact». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Dealings» is a noun, and it is usually used in the plural, with an -s at the end.
fact: «Dealings» means business or contact between people or groups.
fact: «Shady dealings» means dishonest business, often done in secret.
fact: «Honest dealings» means fair, truthful business.
fact: Useful phrases include «have dealings with», «business dealings» and «fair dealings».
exercise: «My dealings with the bank took all morning.» What does dealings mean here? | Money kept safe in the bank | Holidays by the sea | *Business or contact with the bank | Dances held at the bank
exercise: «The police looked into the shady dealings of the company.» What does shady suggest? | Very tall and strong | *Dishonest and secret | Bright and sunny | Friendly and kind
exercise: Mia says, «Her honest dealings with customers made everyone trust her.» What does honest dealings mean? | Business done only at night | Playing cards at a table | Loud shouting at customers | *Fair and truthful business
test: «The two clubs had many dealings over the years.» What does dealings mean? | Fights between them | *Business or contact between them | Games they lost | Gifts they gave away
test: Which phrase means dishonest business? | Friendly visits | Honest business | *Shady dealings | Fair dealings
exam: Which sentence uses dealings correctly? | «The dealings jumped over the moon.» | *«Our dealings with the shop were fair and friendly.» | «Dealings is a big red bird.» | «I dealings my toys to the cat.»
